# Production deployment

Use this procedure when the user explicitly asks to deploy or launch the app in production.

- Host: `root@195.201.98.136`
- App directory: `~/loan-tracker`
- Gunicorn binary: `.venv/bin/gunicorn` (not on system PATH)
- App command:

  ```sh
  .venv/bin/gunicorn --workers 4 --bind 0.0.0.0:8000 --timeout 120 --access-logfile - --error-logfile - app:app
  ```

Deployment sequence (run via SSH as a single remote script):

1. `cd ~/loan-tracker` and `git pull`. Stop and report the error if it fails; do not kill anything if pull fails.
2. Kill any existing loan-tracker gunicorn. **No existing process is valid** — skip kill and continue.
3. Source `.env`, then start gunicorn detached with `nohup`, logging to `/tmp/loan-tracker-gunicorn.log`.
4. Verify processes and port `8000`; report revision and result.

Use this remote script (do not match PIDs with `pgrep -f` against a pattern that also appears in the SSH `bash -c` line — that kills the deploy shell):

```sh
ssh -o BatchMode=yes -o ConnectTimeout=15 root@195.201.98.136 'bash -s' <<'EOF'
set -euo pipefail
cd ~/loan-tracker
git pull

mapfile -t PIDS < <(ps -eo pid=,args= | awk '/\.venv\/bin\/gunicorn .*app:app/ {print $1}')
if ((${#PIDS[@]})); then
  kill "${PIDS[@]}" 2>/dev/null || true
  sleep 2
  mapfile -t PIDS2 < <(ps -eo pid=,args= | awk '/\.venv\/bin\/gunicorn .*app:app/ {print $1}')
  if ((${#PIDS2[@]})); then
    kill -9 "${PIDS2[@]}" 2>/dev/null || true
    sleep 1
  fi
else
  echo "No existing loan-tracker gunicorn found (ok)"
fi

set -a
# shellcheck disable=SC1091
source .env
set +a

nohup .venv/bin/gunicorn --workers 4 --bind 0.0.0.0:8000 --timeout 120 --access-logfile - --error-logfile - app:app > /tmp/loan-tracker-gunicorn.log 2>&1 &
disown || true
sleep 3

ps -eo pid=,args= | awk '/\.venv\/bin\/gunicorn .*app:app/ {print}'
ss -ltnp | grep ':8000' || echo "NOT LISTENING"
git rev-parse --short HEAD
git log -1 --oneline
tail -n 40 /tmp/loan-tracker-gunicorn.log || true
EOF
```

Do not deploy merely because feature work is complete. Deployment is a production mutation and requires an explicit request from the user.

